---
alwaysApply: true
---

Concise rules for building accessible, fast, delightful UIs. Use MUST/SHOULD/NEVER to guide decisions.

## Interactions

### Keyboard & Focus
- MUST: All flows are keyboard-operable, following [WAI-ARIA Authoring Patterns](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/).
- MUST: Every focusable element shows a visible focus ring. Prefer `:focus-visible` over `:focus` to avoid distracting pointer users; use `:focus-within` for grouped controls.
- MUST: Manage focus (trap, move, and return) according to WAI-ARIA patterns.
- MUST: Semantic links (`<a>` or `<Link>`) for navigation to support standard browser behaviors (Cmd/Ctrl+Click, middle-click, right-click). NEVER substitute with `<button>` or `<div>` for navigation.
- SHOULD: Localize keyboard shortcuts for non-QWERTY layouts and show platform-specific symbols.

### Targets & Touch
- MUST: Match visual and hit targets. If visual target is < 24px, MUST expand hit target to ≥ 24px. On mobile, hit target MUST be ≥ 44px.
- MUST: Mobile `<input>` font-size ≥ 16px to prevent iOS Safari auto-zoom, or set `viewport` with `initial-scale=1`.
- MUST: Set `touch-action: manipulation` to prevent double-tap zoom on controls.
- MUST: Set `-webkit-tap-highlight-color` to follow the design.
- NEVER: Disable browser zoom.

### State & Feedback
- MUST: Hydration-safe inputs—must not lose focus or value after hydration.
- MUST: Deep-link everything. URL MUST reflect state (filters, tabs, pagination, expanded panels, `useState`). Use libs like [nuqs](https://nuqs.dev).
- MUST: Back/Forward navigation restores previous scroll positions.
- SHOULD: Optimistic UI—update immediately on success-likely actions, reconcile on server, show error/rollback/undo on failure.
- MUST: Confirm destructive actions or provide an Undo window.
- MUST: Announce async updates with polite `aria-live` for toasts and inline validation.
- SHOULD: Menu options that open follow-ups (e.g., "Rename…") or loading/processing states (e.g., "Saving…") MUST end with an ellipsis character `…`.

### Loading & Timing
- MUST: Loading buttons show a spinner and keep the original label.
- MUST: Add a short show-delay (~150–300ms) and a minimum visible time (~300–500ms) for spinners/skeletons to avoid flicker on fast responses.
- MUST: Delay the first tooltip in a group; subsequent peer tooltips MUST have no delay.

### Scroll & Drag
- MUST: Use intentional `overscroll-behavior: contain` for modals/drawers.
- MUST: Clean drag interactions—disable text selection and apply `inert` to background elements so selection/hover don't occur simultaneously.
- MUST: Design forgiving interactions—generous hit targets, clear affordances, and predictable behavior (e.g., prediction cones).
- MUST: No "dead zones"—if it looks interactive, it MUST be interactive.

## Animation
- MUST: Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` with a reduced-motion variant.
- SHOULD: Prefer CSS > Web Animations API > JavaScript libraries (e.g., motion). Avoid main-thread JS animations when possible.
- MUST: Animate compositor-friendly properties (`transform`, `opacity`). NEVER use `transition: all`.
- MUST: Animations MUST be interruptible by user input and input-driven (avoid autoplay).
- MUST: Set correct `transform-origin` (anchor motion to where it physically starts).
- SHOULD: For SVG, animate `<g>` wrappers and set `transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center` for cross-browser correctness (Safari fixes).

## Layout
- SHOULD: Use optical alignment (adjust ±1px) when perception beats geometry.
- MUST: All alignment is deliberate—to grid, baseline, edge, or optical center; NEVER accidental.
- MUST: Let the browser handle layout—prefer flex/grid/intrinsic flow instead of measuring in JS.
- MUST: Verify on mobile, laptop, and ultra-wide (test ultra-wide at 50% zoom).
- MUST: Respect safe areas (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`) for notches and insets.
- MUST: Avoid unwanted or excessive scrollbars. Test with macOS "Show scroll bars: Always" enabled.
- MUST: Explicitly set image dimensions or reserve space to prevent CLS.

## Content & Accessibility
- SHOULD: Prefer inline help over tooltips.
- MUST: Skeletons MUST mirror final content exactly to prevent layout shift.
- MUST: Accurate `<title>` reflecting the current context.
- MUST: No dead ends—every screen MUST offer a next step or recovery path.
- MUST: Design all states explicitly: empty, sparse, dense, and error.
- SHOULD: Use typographic curly quotes (“ ”) and the ellipsis character `…`.
- MUST: Use tabular numbers for comparisons (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` or Geist Mono).
- MUST: Resilient to user-generated content (short vs very long).
- MUST: Locale-aware formatting for dates, times, numbers, and currencies.
- SHOULD: Detect language via `Accept-Language` header; NEVER rely solely on IP/GPS.
- MUST: Accessible names—use `aria-label` for icon-only buttons, mark decor with `aria-hidden`, and verify in the Accessibility Tree.
- MUST: Prefer native semantics (`button`, `a`, `label`, `table`) over ARIA roles.
- MUST: Use non-breaking spaces `&nbsp;` for glued terms: `10&nbsp;MB`, `⌘&nbsp;+&nbsp;K`, `Vercel&nbsp;SDK`.
- SHOULD: Right-click nav logo surfaces brand assets.

## Forms
- MUST: Enter submits focused text input if it's the only control (or the last one). In `<textarea>`, ⌘/Ctrl+Enter submits, Enter inserts a newline.
- MUST: Every control has a `<label>` (associated by ID). Clicking a label MUST focus the control.
- MUST: Keep submit enabled until request starts; then disable, show spinner, and use an idempotency key. NEVER pre-disable submit; allow submission to surface validation.
- MUST: Don't block typing—accept any input and show validation feedback.
- MUST: No dead zones on checkboxes/radios—label and control MUST share one generous hit target.
- MUST: Errors placed inline next to fields; on submit, focus the first error.
- MUST: Use `autocomplete` with meaningful `name` and correct `type`/`inputmode`.
- MUST: Don't trigger password managers for non-auth fields (like Search). Use `autocomplete="one-time-code"` for OTP.
- MUST: Warn on unsaved changes before navigation.
- MUST: Windows: explicitly set `background-color` and `color` for native `<select>` to avoid dark-mode contrast bugs.

## Performance
- MUST: Measure reliably—disable overhead-adding extensions. Profile with CPU/network throttling.
- MUST: Track and minimize re-renders (React Scan/DevTools).
- MUST: Network latency budget: `POST/PATCH/DELETE` MUST return within < 500ms.
- SHOULD: Prefer uncontrolled inputs; optimize controlled loops for keystroke cost.
- MUST: Virtualize large lists or use `content-visibility: auto`.
- MUST: Preload only above-the-fold images and critical fonts; lazy-load everything else.
- MUST: Subset fonts using `unicode-range`; ship only used code points.
- SHOULD: Move expensive main-thread JS to Web Workers.
- MUST: Use `<link rel="preconnect">` for asset/CDN domains.

## Design
- SHOULD: Layered shadows (min 2 layers) for ambient + direct light.
- SHOULD: Crisp edges—combine semi-transparent borders + shadows.
- SHOULD: Nested radii—child radius ≤ parent radius and concentric.
- SHOULD: Hue consistency—tint borders/shadows/text to match background hue on non-neutral surfaces.
- MUST: Increase contrast on `:hover`, `:active`, and `:focus`.
- MUST: Charts MUST be accessible and color-blind friendly.
- MUST: Meet contrast requirements—prefer [APCA](https://apcacontrast.com/) over WCAG 2.
- MUST: Browser UI MUST match background via `<meta name="theme-color">`.
- MUST: Set `color-scheme` (dark/light) on `<html>` so device UI (scrollbars) matches the theme.
- SHOULD: Avoid gradient banding—use masks if needed.
- SHOULD: Animate wrappers instead of text nodes to avoid smoothing artifacts; use `translateZ(0)` or `will-change: transform` if jank persists.

## Copywriting
- MUST: Use Active Voice ("Install the CLI" vs "The CLI will be installed").
- MUST: Title Case for headings/buttons (Chicago). On marketing, use sentence case.
- MUST: Frame messages positively—errors MUST guide the user to an exit/fix.
- MUST: Use numerals for counts ("8 deployments" vs "eight").
- SHOULD: Prefer `&` over `and`.
- MUST: Separate numbers and units with a space (e.g., `10 MB`).
- MUST: Be clear and concise—use as few words as possible.
- MUST: Use consistent placeholders (Strings: `YOUR_API_TOKEN_HERE`, Numbers: `0123456789`).
- MUST: Write in second person; avoid first person.
- MUST: Consistent nouns—limit unique terms.
- MUST: Consistent currency—don't mix decimal place counts in the same context.